/*
 * Description  : A predicate written at what a zoned collection displays still finds its row
 * Expected Res : Success
 */

// Row 1234 is stored as 1234456 microseconds and displays as 03:00:01.234 in this zone. Pushing that literal
// without converting it back excludes every row group in the file, so this returns nothing rather than too much.
// Asserted on the row returned, because a dropped row is the failure mode.

USE test;

SELECT VALUE r.id FROM RowGroupsZoned r WHERE r.ts = datetime("1970-01-01T03:00:01.234Z");
